Z||000000||DreXteR||05-28-2001||03:47 PM||||I want to make my external balanced engine into an internal balanced engine. What I need to do??  <P>Thanx<P><BR>DreX<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-28-2001||04:05 PM||||You'll need the crank and flywheel/flexplate from an '88 Fiero or most late 80's/early 90's FWD 2.8/3.1 V-6.<P>If you use the FWD stuff you will also need new pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||05-28-2001||04:33 PM||||Correct me if I'm wrong, but the internally balanced engines used larger main bearings than some of the externally balanced ones.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||05-28-2001||06:29 PM||||Wrong. All 2.8 Fieros are large journal. All internall balanced engines are large journal, no compatibility problems.||||reg||1
